'''FunPlus Phoenix''' ''(also known as '''FunPlus X''' or '''FPX''')'' is an esports organization owned by [[:Category:Chinese Teams|Chinese]] game developer [[wikipedia:FunPlus|FunPlus]]. They are most well-known for their ''League of Legends'' division, which entered the LPL ahead of the 2018 season and won a World Championship in just their second year. '''FunPlus Phoenix''' now features teams in ''League of Legends'', ''Fortnite'', ''Call of Duty: Mobile'' and ''VALORANT''. 

Their main VALORANT division formerly competed with a CIS roster before moving their operations to China in 2023 upon the game's release there.

==History==
'''FunPlus Phoenix''' first entered ''VALORANT'' with a mixture of players from [[FABRIKEN]] and [[PartyParrots]]. They were quick to rise to the top, and established themselves as one of the premier European teams within a few months of their creation. 
